            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="1046" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1032"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.4061 Motion Pictures/347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-28T15:00:00+07:00">December 28,
                            1943—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2501. Regarding remittance of earnings of American motion picture companies, your
                    1842, December 22, 11 p.m.;<anchor n="1" xml:id="d772-f1"/> Embassy is <pb
                        facs="1047" n="1033" xml:id="pg1033"/> awaiting precise detailed information
                    from distributors before making approach to Chinese Government. Film
                    distributors have been permitted to remit not more than 50% of their net
                    earnings after deduction of expenses. As to remaining 50%, I question whether
                    film companies here have given careful consideration to probability that they
                    are subject to income and war excess profit taxes, which would affect estimates
                    of amounts available for further remittance. I hope to have precise information
                    from film distributors soon and will then approach Government. Action on behalf
                    of film companies would not be embarrassing as there are no other American
                    interests known to Embassy to be holding funds from [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >for?</hi>] remittance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d772-f1" n="1" xml:id="d772-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; this was a follow-up to the Department’s telegram No. 1604, <hi
